## 6. Acceptance Criteria

P4-01 is PASS only when:

### Guardian identity
- Guardian is a distinct authenticated role.
- Guardian registration is separate from Student registration.
- Guardian verification is enforced before child management.
- Guardian can log in and restore sessions.
- Existing Admin/Teacher/Student authentication continues working.
- Guardian cannot impersonate another role.

### Family Workspace
- A verified Guardian can create a Family Workspace.
- Guardian can access only authorized workspaces.
- One workspace can support multiple Students.
- Multiple Guardians can be associated safely where supported.
- Family Workspace does not inherit School or Teacher privileges.

### Student identity
- Guardian can create a Student without a Teacher or School.
- Student can log in independently.
- Student has one canonical user identity.
- Existing Student accounts remain valid.
- Student can participate in both family and school contexts without duplicate user records.
- Existing assignments, attempts and turns remain attached to the same Student user identity.

### Secure linking
- Guardian can claim a valid invitation for an existing Student.
- Linking does not create a new Student.
- Invalid, expired, revoked and reused tokens fail safely.
- Unauthorized Teachers cannot generate invitations for unrelated Students.
- Guardian cannot discover Student accounts by name or username alone.
- Multiple Guardians can be linked independently.
- Revoking one link does not damage other links or Student data.

### Privacy
- Guardian cannot retrieve answers or turns.
- Guardian cannot retrieve emotion selections.
- Guardian cannot retrieve Body Map or Intensity responses.
- Guardian cannot retrieve Strategy choices or AAC communications.
- Guardian cannot retrieve private Teacher observations.
- Guardian cannot access unlinked Students.
- Guardian cannot access Admin or Teacher functionality.

### Frontend
- Guardian registration/login works with actual backend contracts.
- Guardian portal renders correctly.
- Family Workspace management uses actual backend data.
- Student creation and invitation claiming provide honest success/failure states.
- No fake data is presented as real.

### Regression
- Existing P1/P2/P3 backend and frontend tests remain passing.
- TypeScript passes.
- Production build passes.
- New Guardian tests pass.
- Database health remains healthy.
- No migration is executed.
- No live database mutation occurs.

Use `PASS`, `FAIL` and `NOT RUN` honestly.

A missing email provider, browser, live Guardian credentials or disposable test database must be reported as `NOT RUN` or a clearly identified operational dependency. Do not fake successful verification.

